id:                     E371
trigger_tool: tar|python|powershell|runtime
phase: validation|readback|postrelease
error_signature: terminal readback tar closure invalid|unsafe or duplicate readback member|archive directory set drift
severity: 2
category: readback-archive-contract
match_keywords: tar, readback, directory member, archive root, trailing slash, terminal evidence, postrelease, SHA-256
title: Validate directory-rooted readback archives by exact member type sets
root_cause: Archiving a result directory by name emits mandatory root and subdirectory records, but a regular-file-only predicate or pathname regex can reject those valid directory members after the target and release already completed.
affected_scope: Host validators that consume task result tar archives after one-shot device execution and sealed release.
verification_cmd: Validate the exact directory and regular-file sets, reject links and unexpected members, verify every evidence manifest hash, and bind terminal, release, postrelease, and transport identities.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: exact-directory-and-regular-file-whitelists
rec_description: Separate directory and regular-file contracts, require canonical unique in-root names, verify sizes and hashes only for regular files, and preserve the consumed failure while reconciling a proven postrelease PASS without relaunch.
rec_command: python -B validate_readback.py --tar result-readback.tar --attempt-root attempt --claim-root claim --output reconciliation.json
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: create-new-validator-successor-before-release
fallback_description: If remote release has not completed, preserve the failed controller and use a new independently audited validator and release path; never patch or rerun the consumed generation.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: not member.isfile\(\)|regular-file regex.*all tar members
forbid_1_reason: A directory-rooted archive legitimately contains directory records with trailing slashes and no payload.
forbid_1_consequence: A successful target and release can be misclassified as a corrupt readback.
forbid_2_pattern: retry.*run-once|second launch|rewrite.*failure-result
forbid_2_reason: A postrelease host validator defect does not restore the consumed one-launch authority.
forbid_2_consequence: The target workload can execute twice and immutable failure evidence can be falsified.
